 "visits": {
  "20": "Bring 10 bandages, Lullaby and Artemisia potions and comfrey for In God's Hands; it's timed, and First Aid III helps.",
  "45": "Have 60 groschen and potions for the tourney, an antidote for Black Peter's poisoned blade, and Reading for Money for Old Rope.",
  "46": "Be ready to ride with Bernard to Neuhof immediately; he won't wait. First Aid II lets you bandage Jakub.",
  "48": "On the Scent is timed: head out promptly or Runt's men reach Reeky first.",
  "50": "Bring a torch, Bane/poison potions, good armour, plenty of potions, and arrive rested and fed for the Pribyslavitz assault.",
  "56": "Hunting 5 with Butcher, a bow and a big-pack horse for the Huntsman job; lockpicks for Cherchez la Femme; Lukesh's delivery is two-day timed.",
  "57": "The quarry wages heist runs on a five-day clock. Start Gallows Brothers only for Andrew's dialogue — it's meant to fail at The Die is Cast.",
  "60": "Race on Zora's grey with good spurs and an Aesop potion; pace the horse's stamina.",
  "62": "At Your Service is timed; bring lockpicks and a bow for the errands and bandits.",
  "72": "Bring a torch for the silver mine and expect hostile miners.",
  "85": "Lockpicking for Very Hard chests is needed throughout All that Glisters.",
  "87": "Interlopers' bandits are well armoured: bring poison, potions, lockpicks, top gear and a horse.",
  "93": "Rebuilding Pribyslavitz needs roughly 10,800 groschen upfront plus daily wages; Speech above 17 helps with Marius.",
  "95": "For the Capon quests bring dice, noble clothing, lockpicks and good Speech; Next to Godliness must finish by morning.",
  "101": "Join the fight club through the Sasau tanner, then report to Radzig before you enter the monastery.",
  "104": "Your belongings are confiscated at the gate; plan on Speech to get lockpicks from Cellarius. Finish any side quests you care about — Vranik is next.",
  "106": "Collect the Pirkstein armoury kit if your gear wasn't recovered; expect a large battle.",
  "107": "Wear quiet night gear with a Nighthawk potion; gather 60 mint, 30 valerian, 6 wormwood for the Cockerel potions.",
  "110": "Bring at least 300 groschen and healing potions; you need Unarmed 8 to face the King of the Cumans.",
  "111": "Wear high-quality armour for Erik and the trebuchet defence; Speech and Charisma pay off in his interrogation."
 },
 "acts": {
  "1": "Starting stats: no reading, no lockpicking, no horse. Avoid fights — Theresa's chapter is pitched around level 4–5.",
  "2": "Reading learned, Hard locks open (Very Hard needs Lockpicking 15), Hunting 5 with Butcher, First Aid perks, padded armour. Still on foot.",
  "3": "Tourney-capable after Bernard's training, Pebbles as your horse, decent armour, and potions and poison ready for Pribyslavitz.",
  "4": "Hunting 5+ with Butcher and the Gamekeeper perk, Speech near 15, and a camp-clearing kit: Bane potions, a dagger, lockpicks.",
  "5": "Strong armour and Speech for Kuno's band, Reading for Last Will, and savings building towards Pribyslavitz (~10,800 groschen).",
  "6": "Very Hard lockpicking, solid Drinking, First Aid II, noble clothes for Capon, top armour for Interlopers.",
  "7": "Very Hard lockpicking and good Speech for the monastery, where you have no gear. Side quests wrapped up before Vranik.",
  "8": "Endgame: quiet night gear and Nighthawk for the raid, high-quality armour for Erik, and Cockerel ingredients for the siege."
 }
}